              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वेतनम् — vetanam — \"wages, salary\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "vetana \"wages, hire, salary\" appears from Manu on. The grammarians derive it from √vī, while MW thinks it rather belongs with √vṛt \"turn\" and vartana \"livelihood\", so its origin is uncertain."
            }
          ]
        },
